	(text ".model SWMOD SW(Ron=5m Roff=1e6 Vt=2.5 Vh=0.1)\nK1 L1 L2 0.9999\n.tran 20n 400u 300u"
		(at 40 210 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "14f834f3-f316-41b1-8e1e-f32500f001ec")
	)
	(text "DUAL ACTIVE BRIDGE  -  48 V Mako pack  <->  400 V link,  3 kW,  single phase shift\n\nL3 = 56 uH is the customer-supplied series inductance on the HIGH-voltage side of the\nPCB-coil planar transformer. It is what sets power transfer, with the turns ratio and\nthe switching frequency:   P = V1 * (V2/n) * phi * (pi - phi) / (2 * pi^2 * f * L)\n\nL1 / L2 are the transformer, n = 8.33 (L2/L1 = n^2), K1 couples them at 0.9999 so the\nleakage is L3 and nothing else.  f = 100 kHz.  phi = 54 deg  ->  VG3/VG4 delayed 1.5 us.\n\nD1-D8 are the body diodes. They are not decoration: without a freewheel path the\n100 ns dead time chops the inductor current and the transfer falls from 3.0 kW to\n1.2 kW. Deleting them does not make the model simpler, it makes it wrong.\n\nSimulated: 3016 W in, 2943 W out, 97.6%.  Closed form: 3001 W.  Agreement 0.5%."
		(at 40 225 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "01c9c1bc-f29b-431b-aa70-161918bdbcaf")
	)
